                        "entry_id": "ad457bd9-2081-366a-957a-0601ee6f8179",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Characterized by heavy bass sounds."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "db632b6d-0c52-4fa5-b924-af1235be32ba",
                                "sense_id": "d40a66ce-4a56-37d5-b148-f03a25e70404",
                                "text": "If you're miking a boomy acoustic, the proximity effect can work against you, but having it on a thin-sounding arch-top can work for you."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "655dbd07-4512-4d3a-902c-99ba1c29ba89",
                                "sense_id": "d40a66ce-4a56-37d5-b148-f03a25e70404",
                                "text": "As an airliner approaches you from a long way off, the sound is first heard as rumble, and, as it get closer and then directly overhead, the sound becomes increasingly boomier."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3984cafc-397d-4a97-9251-f10357e8d74c",
                                "sense_id": "d40a66ce-4a56-37d5-b148-f03a25e70404",
                                "text": "For the third movement Mr. Safronov had Schubert’s piano sketch as a guide, but his big, boomy orchestration, with a gentle pastoral trio at its core, sounded jarring after the first two movements."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8b185a24-6a9d-3cd9-a233-4062a6df32a7",
                        "entry_id": "ad457bd9-2081-366a-957a-0601ee6f8179",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of or pertaining to a financial boom, resources boom, baby boom, etc."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "964052ea-8fd7-435e-987e-91f815027d82",
                                "sense_id": "8b185a24-6a9d-3cd9-a233-4062a6df32a7",
                                "text": "c. 1880s, Rudyard Kipling, quoted in 1992, John William Reps, The Making of Urban America: A History of City Planning in the United States, page 412,\nTacoma was literally staggering under a boom of the boomiest. I do not quite remember what her natural resources were supposed to be, […] ."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "baa5d88f-e869-4bf0-83a5-427ab0576b75",
                                "sense_id": "8b185a24-6a9d-3cd9-a233-4062a6df32a7",
                                "text": "A larger amount of capital is seeking investment than in the boomiest of boom times, yet there is no boom now."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3522e3f7-95ff-47fa-ad0d-800b4a390b5f",
                                "sense_id": "8b185a24-6a9d-3cd9-a233-4062a6df32a7",
                                "text": "Even in boomier times, the flexibility that leasing provides has become increasingly important to companies."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
